1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:15,347
Professor: Os regulares pegam 'ed', lembra? Mas os verbos mais comuns são REBELDES — mudam de cara. São só três campeões, e eu vou trazer eles de novo e de novo até grudarem. 'go' vira 'went'. E ó, 'pra casa' é só 'home', sem 'to'. 'eu fui pra casa':

2
00:00:15,847 --> 00:00:16,869
Professor: I went home.

3
00:00:18,095 --> 00:00:19,302
Bia: I went home.

4
00:00:21,278 --> 00:00:24,111
Professor: 'ter' vira 'had'. 'eu tinha um carro':

5
00:00:24,611 --> 00:00:25,772
Professor: I had a car.

6
00:00:27,575 --> 00:00:28,690
Bia: I had a car.

7
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:36,089
Professor: E 'dizer' vira 'said' — e repara o som, encolhe pra 'séd'. 'ela disse isso':

8
00:00:36,589 --> 00:00:37,518
Professor: She said it.

9
00:00:39,279 --> 00:00:40,579
Bia: She said it.

10
00:00:41,079 --> 00:00:47,256
Bia: Ah — então esses não pegam 'ed', é só ir pegando a cara nova com o uso? went, had, said?

11
00:00:48,906 --> 00:01:00,191
Professor: Isso — são os rebeldes, cada um com a cara dele, sem regra; eu vou repetindo até virar automático. E o contraste: 'I go' agora, 'I went' antes. 'eles foram pra casa':

12
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:04,467
Bia: They went home.

13
00:01:05,603 --> 00:01:06,857
Professor: 'você tinha um carro':

14
00:01:10,281 --> 00:01:11,442
Bia: You had a car.

15
00:01:13,682 --> 00:01:14,704
Professor: 'ele disse isso':

16
00:01:17,827 --> 00:01:18,849
Bia: He said it.

17
00:01:20,183 --> 00:01:21,623
Professor: 'ela tinha um problema':

18
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:26,597
Bia: She had a problem.

19
00:01:29,018 --> 00:01:30,179
Professor: 'eles disseram isso':

20
00:01:33,756 --> 00:01:34,963
Bia: They said it.

21
00:01:36,558 --> 00:01:37,719
Professor: 'eu fui lá ontem':

22
00:01:41,695 --> 00:01:43,553
Bia: I went there yesterday.

23
00:01:44,622 --> 00:01:49,220
Professor: Agora mistura com o 'ed' dos regulares: 'eu trabalhei ontem, e eu fui pra casa':

24
00:01:53,078 --> 00:01:55,772
Bia: I worked yesterday, and I went home.

25
00:01:57,206 --> 00:01:59,296
Professor: 'eu tava cansado, então eu fui pra casa':

26
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:04,623
Bia: I was tired, so I went home.

27
00:02:05,799 --> 00:02:08,214
Professor: Agora rápido, cuidado com o rebelde: 'eu fui':

28
00:02:11,522 --> 00:02:12,404
Bia: I goed?

29
00:02:12,904 --> 00:02:17,223
Bia: ...não, peraí — 'go' é rebelde, não pega 'ed'. É 'went'. I went.

30
00:02:18,494 --> 00:02:21,745
Professor: Cravou — 'go' vira 'went', sem 'ed'. De novo:

31
00:02:25,326 --> 00:02:26,394
Bia: I went.

32
00:02:28,352 --> 00:02:33,135
Professor: Recombina, trazendo o 'ter' no passado: 'ele tinha um carro, mas ele não tá aqui agora':

33
00:02:36,507 --> 00:02:39,108
Bia: He had a car, but he isn't here now.

34
00:02:40,929 --> 00:02:42,833
Professor: 'ela disse isso, mas eu não entendo':

35
00:02:45,895 --> 00:02:48,728
Bia: She said it, but I don't understand.

36
00:02:49,817 --> 00:02:52,278
Professor: 'nós estávamos lá, e nós fomos pra casa':

37
00:02:55,483 --> 00:02:57,991
Bia: We were there, and we went home.

38
00:03:00,011 --> 00:03:01,265
Professor: 'nós fomos lá ontem':

39
00:03:04,692 --> 00:03:06,364
Bia: We went there yesterday.

40
00:03:07,835 --> 00:03:09,971
Professor: E fecha: 'eu fui pra casa ontem':

41
00:03:13,556 --> 00:03:15,228
Bia: I went home yesterday.

42
00:03:16,907 --> 00:03:31,443
Professor: Sacou? Os comuns são irregulares no passado — 'go' vira 'went', 'have' vira 'had', 'say' vira 'said', sem 'ed'; mais uns vêm com o uso. E pra NEGAR e PERGUNTAR no passado? Tem um ajudante — vem já.

43
00:03:32,892 --> 00:03:39,301
Bia: Boa — 'I went home'. Os rebeldes vão grudando; o resto pega 'ed'. Agora eu conto o que já foi!

